# GitHub Actions deploy secrets (Settings → Secrets → Actions)
#
# FTP_SERVER        Hostname ONLY — e.g. ftp.zhengkyc.com (no ftp:// prefix)
# FTP_USERNAME      cPanel FTP username
# FTP_PASSWORD      cPanel FTP password
# FTP_SERVER_DIR    e.g. /public_html/ispbilling/  (trailing slash)
# DEPLOY_EXTRACT_TOKEN  Random string for /deploy-extract-vendor.php?token=
#
# FTP_PROTOCOL (important — fixes "Timeout control socket"):
#   ftps          ← try FIRST (most cPanel hosts, port 21)
#   sftp          ← if host only allows SFTP (port 22)
#   ftp           ← plain FTP, rarely works from GitHub
#   ftps-legacy   ← implicit FTPS (port 990)
# FTP_PORT        21 (ftps), 22 (sftp), or 990 (ftps-legacy)
#
# Manual test: Actions → Deploy to production → Run workflow → pick protocol
#
# If port preflight fails: host blocks GitHub Actions IPs — ask host to allow,
# or deploy code via cPanel File Manager / FileZilla from your PC only.
#
# Workflows:
#   1) Deploy to production (FTP) — app code on every push
#   2) Upload vendor (FTP chunks) — manual, then browser extract URL
#
# No terminal on server: use cPanel File Manager to upload vendor.zip
#   (run .\scripts\build-vendor-zip.ps1 on your PC first)
